  (text "GD1\nRRIO op-amp on WHITE rail\n(0-16V, input CMR must reach V+)\ne.g. TI LM7321 (RRIO, 2.5-32V)" (at 138 104 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "Rsense\n0.1 ohm\n(WHITE leg)\n0.3V at 3A" (at 176 106 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "Q1\nTIP147 PNP Darlington\nTO-220 + heatsink\n(or N-MOSFET alt:\nSUP70060E/RFP50N06)" (at 191 103 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "D4\nMBRS360\nreverse block" (at 208 122 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "DAC2 level translator\nR_KA1 6.8k/R_KA2 1.2k + GD3 LM7321\n(KA_DAC_DEMAND from MCU DAC2 DC)" (at 120 134 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "ANTI-BRAKE = CONSTANT-CURRENT SOURCE (this revision):\nClassic high-side op-amp current source. GD1 drives Q1 and regulates the drop across\nRsense (0.1 ohm) to equal the demand, holding I = Vdemand/Rsense regardless of motor.\nDemand: MCU DAC2 DC, scaled by R_KA1/R_KA2 divider + GD3 (LM7321) to 0-0.3V referred to WHITE.\nPot sets DAC code -> current. code 0 = 0A (off); full = 3A.\nWhy a current source: a stalled motor (start line) is ~short; a voltage source would\ndump unbounded current. A current source bounds it to ~3A - correct, and matches\nreal controllers (Kobic etc). Replaces the retired voltage follower (TIP122)." (at 15 95 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "THERMAL (steady-state baseline, from SIMetrix design):\nVsupply max 16V, Ta 30C. At 2.75A -> Pd 44W (47W at full 3A).\nTIP147: SOA 125W@25C, Tj allow 125C, Rthjc 1C/W -> Rthca 1.16C/W, Tc 81C.\nSUP70060E: SOA 200W, Tj 150C, Rthjc 0.75 -> Rthca 1.98C/W, Tc 117C (smaller sink, hotter).\nAnti-brake is bursty: size heatsink by pulse energy / thermal capacitance\n(dT ~= Energy/Cth) not steady 47W - a ~50g Al sink (Cth ~45 J/C) rises ~2C per 2s burst." (at 15 132 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "OP-AMP SUPPLY - CRITICAL:\nGD1 is powered from the WHITE rail (~16V), NOT +5V. Rsense is in the WHITE leg,\nso the op-amp inputs/output sit at ~16V common mode; a 5V op-amp cannot work here.\nUse a RAIL-TO-RAIL INPUT op-amp whose input CMR includes V+ (e.g. TI LM7321, SOT-23, 2.5-32V RRIO).\nOrdinary LM358/LM321/LM324 stop ~1.5V below V+ and will NOT work here.\nConfirmed by the SIMetrix design (op-amp V+ = supply rail). Only GD2 (brake) is on +5V." (at 15 150 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "SAFETY:\nShoot-through protection - if brake (Q2) and anti-brake fault on together, the\ncurrent source caps its contribution at ~3A instead of feeding a near-short.\nAdd open/short detection on the loop + fast OCP to guard source component failure." (at 15 165 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
  (text "RETIRED - do NOT fit: floating-supply P-ch (ZD1/R_Z1/C_Z1/LM321, IRF9Z34N) and the\nvoltage-follower TIP122 NPN; 2N2222 PWM level-shift + C_KA RC filter (now DAC2 + GD3). See design doc 7A.7." (at 15 188 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))
)
